 "notes": {
  "weeks": "FY W34..W41 (Mon-Sun), Mondays 2026-08-24 to 2026-10-12; LY L38..L41 = Mondays 2025-09-22 to 2025-10-13 at -364 days. USA FY = calendar year, W1 Monday 5 Jan 2026.",
  "bookings": "CREATE PATH ONLY, new basis from this week: andGroup(eventName EXACT 'sevenrooms_booking_complete', NOT pagePath PARTIAL_REGEXP 'modify|manage|prearrival'). Aqua NYC additionally AND pagePath PARTIAL_REGEXP 'aquanyc|aquakyotonyc'.",
  "ytd_window": "2026-01-01..2026-10-18, rebuilt on the create path (18,681 market) against 20,104 published to 11 Oct on the old basis.",
  "GA4_BOOKING_EVENT_FAILURE": "Discovered this run. sevenrooms_booking_complete stops firing across all three USA properties mid-week. Market create-path bookings by day 12-18 Oct: 74, 65, 64, 50, 2, 2, 1. By venue on 16/17/18 Oct: Aqua Roma 2/1/0, Aqua Kyoto 0/0/0, Hutong NYC 0/0/1, Hutong Miami 0/1/0. Hutong NYC fell on 15 Oct (5 vs 20 the day before). Sessions on 16-18 Oct were normal (Aqua 903/866/604, Hutong NYC 793/742/287, Hutong Miami 499/652/476). SevenRooms website bookings on the same three days were 43/43/39 (125 bookings, 378 covers) and Meta Schedule conversions rose week on week at all three venues. Conclusion: measurement failure, not demand. The week's GA4 figure of 258 is a four-day reading and is published as pulled, not grossed up.",
  "amendment_share": "2026 week: market 15 of 273 booking events on modify/manage/prearrival = 5.5%. Aqua NYC 0 of 151 = 0%; Hutong NYC 6 of 73 = 8.2% (4 modify + 2 prearrival); Hutong Miami 9 of 49 = 18.4%. 2025 week: Aqua NYC property 70 of 420 = 16.7% (70 of its own 347 venue rows = 20.2%); Hutong NYC 0 of 163; Hutong Miami 0 of 76. In Oct 2025 both Hutongs still fired the event on the /reservations/<venue> landing route with no modify variant, so the amendment distortion in the USA last year is confined to Aqua NYC. Prior week 2026: market 35 of 419 = 8.4% (Aqua 0 of 206, Hutong NYC 20 of 146, Hutong Miami 9 of 67).",
  "aqua_nyc_cross_tagging": "Found this run. In the year-ago week the Aqua NYC property (451165443) recorded 73 sevenrooms_booking_complete events on /reservations/hutongnewyork* paths (40 + 18 + 11 + 2 + 2), which are also counted in the Hutong New York property. Aqua NYC is therefore restricted to pagePath 'aquanyc|aquakyotonyc' in both years. Unrestricted create-path property total for the year-ago week is 350 against the 277 published here. The 2026 week carries no such rows.",
  "hutong_nyc_ly_gap": "Re-verified this run. A daily pull of sevenrooms_booking_complete for 6-26 Oct 2025 returns no rows before 15 Oct 2025 and then 40, 38, 35, 25, 25 on 15-19 Oct. The year-ago week 13-19 Oct 2025 therefore has five of seven days and 163 bookings on 5,269 sessions. Not like for like, so the venue's YoY is withheld again, this time as a partial-week gap rather than a total outage.",
  "aqua_kyoto_new_venue_flag": "The standing position is that Aqua Kyoto NYC is new in 2026 with no 2025 data, and the trends page follows it. The data does not support it: create-path booking events on /explore/aquakyotonyc/ exist through Sep and Oct 2025 (L38 82, L39 105, L40 75, L41 85). Raised rather than relitigated. If the position changes, Aqua Kyoto gets a real YoY line and Aqua Roma's continuation line must stop including Kyoto's 2025.",
  "series_provenance": "Bookings W34..W41 and L38..L41 all pulled daily this run and summed on the create path, so the whole visible series is on one basis. Weekly single-window users W34..W39 carried from the published w2026-10-05 raw file; W40 and W41 pulled this run. W40 restated up: Aqua NYC 6,680 to 6,707, Hutong NYC 3,864 to 3,892, Hutong Miami 2,833 to 2,853; Aqua Kyoto 1,031 to 1,033.",
  "ga4_engagement_restatement": "Prior-week session metrics restated again: Aqua NYC sessions 7,907 to 7,959, average session duration 151.4 to 135.5, bounce 0.426 to 0.433; Hutong NYC bounce 0.470 to 0.372; Hutong Miami bounce 0.605 to 0.535. Read the current week's bounce and engagement as provisional."
 }
